# Conformance output is never committed. A gap report names which repos lack
# protection, which guards do not check anything, and where work is stranded --
# an inventory of soft spots. The value is in the tool, not in the findings.
# This entry exists before the first report is ever generated: a file that was
# briefly committed and then removed is still in history and still public.
